      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَصَابَهَ لفْحٌ مِنْ حَرُورٍ وَسَمُومٍ</span></b>  <i>A burning gust of
hot night-wind, and of hot day-wind, smote him.</i>
(L.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَصَابَهُ مِنَ الحَرِّ لَفْحٌ وَمِنَ البَرْدِ نَفْحٌ</span> [<i>A
blast of heat smote him, and a blast of cold</i>]. (A.)
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  You say also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَوَافِحُ السَّمُوِم</span> [pl. of ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَافِحَةٌ</span></b> ,
and meaning <i>Burning blasts of the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سموم</span>]. (S,
K in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سفع</span>.)

